{
  "about": "Twenty claims whose answers were worked out by hand from the policy wording (data/rules.json) and the standard age depreciation schedule (0 to 6 months nil, to 1 year 5%, to 2 years 10%, to 3 years 15%, to 4 years 25%, to 5 years 35%, to 10 years 40%, over 10 years 50%), NOT produced by running the engine. The existing golden labels were generated by the same code they test, so they cannot catch a rule that is wrong in both places. These can. Every case sits on a boundary. Vehicle age is days from 1 June of the registration year to the incident, divided by 365. Money rounds to the nearest rupee, halves up.",
